  "step_2": "The individual considered the possibility of not incurring losses (i.e., no negative outcomes) and emphasized the higher potential gain (4000 Euros) despite its lower probability. The individual expressed a preference for the option with the higher reward, even though it has a lower chance of being realized. The justification centers on the potential for a larger gain and the absence of loss, without any mention of the distribution of probabilities or the relative skewness of the lotteries. The individual did not refer to the concentration of probability on unfavorable outcomes or compare the degree of skewness between the two lotteries.",
  "step_3": "The decision reason requires evaluating skewness based on the relative weight of unfavorable outcomes. The individual did not mention skewness, probability distribution, or the comparison of unfavorable probability mass. Instead, the justification focused on the absence of loss and the higher potential gain, which aligns more with a focus on maximum possible outcome or risk aversion, not skewness. While both lotteries are right-skewed, the individual did not use the relative degree of skewness as a criterion. The reasoning process described does not reflect the application of the skewness-based rule. Therefore, the decision reason was not used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
